 "decisions": "CRITICAL (data-part-critical, DD-149): studio-lt-revert (focus-mode revert button: replaces everything written since focus mode opened with the opened text; the way back is one history step, but no Undo toast is offered) and studio-lt-replace-all (replace all: rewrites every match in one go). Both are single icon buttons without part-bearing children, so there are no protected children (criticalChildren is empty). Their ancestors are therefore NOT safe: studio-lt-focus, studio-lt-focus-tools, studio-lt-focus-toolbar-end, studio-lt-find, studio-lt-find-replace-row. Everything else is safe: it is never a critical element, never inside one and never contains one.\nNOT critical, with reasons: card delete (menu item; the change shows the shell's Undo toast, which is already studio-undo-toast critical); card split, convert to start block, move, duplicate, make main (swap; nothing is dropped, each is one history step); paste-many sheet (appends new cards, replaces nothing; ordinary sheet, kind lt-paste); macro sheet (inserts at the caret; ordinary sheet, kind lt-macros); problem one-click fix (replaces one old-form macro with its new form, one history step, like a spelling suggestion; the author can see the text); replace one (a single match, selected and visible); sandbox 'copy chat values' (changes sandbox values only, never the author's data); cap-grip reset. If the maintainer wants more caution, the first candidates to promote are the problem fix and replace one (each needs its own part name and would make studio-lt-problem and studio-lt-find-row unsafe ancestors).\nLT inside slice 4: the editor is mounted in slice 4 forms by st4-core.js mountLT, which overwrites the data-part of three of my elements: the wrapper (studio-lt-field becomes studio-field-control), the label span (studio-lt-label becomes studio-field-label) and the chip host (studio-lt-chip-host becomes studio-field-chip; drawChip only sets a name when none is there). All other studio-lt-* parts and all state attributes stay. No LT field can sit inside studio-risky (that section holds switches only), inside a question sheet or any other critical element: the field markup is only built in #formHost / focus mode, and the shared sheet's body is rebuilt on every open.\nNot given a part (aria-hidden or per-token): highlight spans inside the mirror (class c1..c11, em, mk: colours stay tokens), the hidden measuring twins (lt-probe, lt-measure), the sr-only description, the spacer span (lt-sp), the plain wrappers .lt-textv > .fld and the paste sheet's display: contents wrapper, small icons, the demo-panel controls (#ltDemo, mockup chrome). Not changed: the focus mode's 'more' menu offers revert as an ordinary menu item of the shared sheet (slice1.js openMenu), so that copy of revert is not critical (see the report)."
